                <pb facs="0887" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg799"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bay to Mr. Eddy.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay informs Mr. Eddy that Bear-Admiral Charles Henry Davis has been
                    appointed by the President as a member of the North Sea Commission, and asks to
                    be informed as to the date his presence will be required in Paris.)</p>
            </div>
